  "findings": [
    "1.6.1 trains `SingleDrugRandomForest` once per drug with `random_state` unset (global numpy stream); v2 pins `random_state=42` in the predictor and builds one forest per drug from it. With `random_state` equal to the integer the global stream is seeded with before each drug, the per-drug forests are identical (feature importances and predictions exact).",
    "Same scaler deviation as `SingleDrugElasticNet`: 1.6.1 standardizes with the training samples of the drug, v2 with all training samples (plan 4.4). With a shared sample set the features agree to float32 precision.",
    "Defaults agree: 1.6.1 first grid point n_estimators=100, max_samples=0.2, max_depth=5 (grid 5/10/30); v2 declares n_estimators=100, max_samples=0.2, max_depth=5, n_jobs=-1. Only `random_state` differs (unset vs 42). The `defaults` variant runs the unmodified preset against 1.6.1 with its global stream seeded with 42.",
    "1.6.1 selects `landmark_genes` while loading; the v2 preset selects the same list with `scaledGeneExpression(gene_list=landmark_genes)`. The synthetic gene names are in no shipped list, so both sides get a pre-selected matrix and the selection itself is not compared here."
  ],
